WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.800
Relationships describe how many rows can connect

00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:07.430
between entities In a one-to-one relationship each

00:00:07.456 --> 00:00:09.246
side connects to at most one row

00:00:09.272 --> 00:00:12.750
on the other side In a one-to-many

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:15.368
relationship one parent can connect to many

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:18.384
child rows A patient can have many

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.660
appointments so the foreign key belongs on

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:25.177
the appointment side In a many-to-many relationship

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.559
both sides can connect to many rows

00:00:28.482 --> 00:00:31.140
Appointments can contain many services and a

00:00:31.153 --> 00:00:35.524
service can appear in many appointments Relational

00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:38.590
databases resolve that many-to-many relationship
with a

00:00:38.616 --> 00:00:42.589
junction table The placement rule is worth

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:45.734
remembering conceptually in one-to-many put the
foreign

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:48.842
key on the many side In many-to-many

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:51.578
introduce an intersection or junction table
